key.categories.steinlens=Stein
key.steinlens.zoom=Zoom
key.steinlens.zoomSecondary=Second Zoom
steinlens.button=Lens...
steinlens.dynamicFov=Dynamic FOV
steinlens.dynamicFov.hint=The field of view widens when sprinting or with Speed and narrows when drawing a bow, as in the game. Off, it always stays the same
steinlens.motionBlur=Motion blur
steinlens.motionBlur.hint=Motion: the image blurs along the way the camera moves, sharp the moment it stops. Trail: what moves leaves a short trail, as in other clients. The HUD and the hand never blur, and it looks the same at any frame rate
steinlens.motionBlur.0=Off
steinlens.motionBlur.1=Motion
steinlens.motionBlur.2=Trail
steinlens.motionBlurStrength=Blur strength
steinlens.motionBlurStrength.hint=How long the blur is: 1 barely shows, 10 is strong
steinlens.zoom=Zoom
steinlens.zoom.hint=Hold %s to zoom. Change the key in Controls, under Stein
steinlens.zoomSmooth=Smooth camera on zoom
steinlens.zoomSmooth.hint=The camera moves smoothly while zooming
steinlens.zoomFactor=Zoom level
steinlens.zoomFactor.hint=How many times closer the zoom brings the view
steinlens.zoomToggle=Press to toggle
steinlens.zoomToggle.hint=On: a press of the key zooms and the next one goes back. Off: the zoom lasts while the key is held
steinlens.zoomInMs=Zoom in time
steinlens.zoomInMs.hint=How long the view takes to get all the way in. Instant: at once, as before
steinlens.zoomOutMs=Zoom out time
steinlens.zoomOutMs.hint=How long the view takes to go back. Instant: at once, as before
steinlens.zoomInstant=Instant
steinlens.ms=%s ms
steinlens.zoomCurve=Transition curve
steinlens.zoomCurve.hint=How the zoom moves during its time: at a constant speed, slow at both ends, or fast at the start
steinlens.zoomCurve.linear=Linear
steinlens.zoomCurve.smooth=Smooth
steinlens.zoomCurve.easeOut=Ease out
steinlens.zoomCurve.easeOutStrong=Strong ease out
steinlens.zoomScroll=Scroll to change the level
steinlens.zoomScroll.hint=While zoomed, the scroll wheel brings the view closer or farther and the hotbar slot stays the same
steinlens.zoomScrollStep=Step per notch
steinlens.zoomScrollStep.hint=How much each notch of the wheel changes the zoom level
steinlens.zoomScrollMin=Lowest level
steinlens.zoomScrollMin.hint=The wheel does not take the zoom below this level
steinlens.zoomScrollMax=Highest level
steinlens.zoomScrollMax.hint=The wheel does not take the zoom above this level
steinlens.zoomScrollSmooth=Smooth level change
steinlens.zoomScrollSmooth.hint=The level glides to the one the wheel chose instead of jumping
steinlens.zoomScrollRemember=Keep the scrolled level
steinlens.zoomScrollRemember.hint=The next zoom starts at the level the wheel left, instead of the key's own
steinlens.zoomShowLevel=Show the level when scrolling
steinlens.zoomShowLevel.hint=The zoom level appears above the hotbar when the wheel changes it
steinlens.zoomLevelShown=Zoom: %s
steinlens.zoomSecondaryFactor=Second zoom level
steinlens.zoomSecondaryFactor.hint=The level of the second zoom key, which starts with no key. Choose it in Controls, under Stein
steinlens.zoomScaleSensitivity=Slower mouse while zoomed
steinlens.zoomScaleSensitivity.hint=The mouse turns the view less the closer the zoom, so aiming feels the same as without it
steinlens.zoomHideHand=Hide the hand while zoomed
steinlens.zoomHideHand.hint=The held item and the arm are not drawn while the zoom is on
steinlens.customItems=Enchantment textures
steinlens.customItems.hint=Different textures for items and armour by enchantment, when the resource pack has them. Rules in the current pack: %s
steinlens.glint=Glint
steinlens.glint.near=Near only
steinlens.glint.hint=The shine of enchanted items. Near only: hidden on armour and items farther than %s blocks; in your hand and inventory it always shows
steinlens.armor=Armor
steinlens.armor.shown=Shown
steinlens.armor.hidden=Hidden
steinlens.armor.hint=Hides the armour worn by players and mobs, yours included. On your screen only
steinlens.nametags=Nametags
steinlens.nametags.default=Default
steinlens.nametags.blocks=%s blocks
steinlens.nametags.hint=How far the names over players and mobs show (the game shows them up to 64 blocks)
steinlens.default=Default
steinlens.compactAngles=Compact angles
steinlens.compactAngles.hint=Uses a smaller table for the animations' maths, which the processor reads faster. Animations get slightly less precise
steinlens.fog=Fog
steinlens.fog.light=Light
steinlens.fog.hint=The fog at the edge of the distance. Light: only at the edge. Water, lava and blindness do not change
steinlens.cloudHeight=Cloud height
steinlens.cloudHeight.blocks=+%s blocks
steinlens.cloudHeight.hint=Raises the clouds above the game's usual height (128), so they do not cut through tall builds
steinlens.keep=Extended distance
steinlens.keep.memory=Memory
steinlens.keep.disk=Disk
steinlens.keep.hint=Chunks the server drops stay on screen up to your distance. Disk: kept per server, they come back on the next visit. Changing worlds clears the memory
steinlens.keepLimit=Storage limit
steinlens.keepLimit.hint=How much terrain to keep. Past the limit, the farthest (memory) or the oldest (disk) goes first
steinlens.connectedTextures=Connected blocks
steinlens.connectedTextures.hint=The resource pack's connected textures (glass, bookshelves...), seamless between equal blocks. Rules in the current pack: %s
steinlens.chunkUploads=Chunks per frame
steinlens.chunkUploads.hint=How many new chunks go to the graphics card per frame. With a limit, terrain appears more slowly but without stutters
steinlens.waitNeighbors=Wait for neighbors
steinlens.waitNeighbors.hint=Only draws a chunk once its neighbours have arrived: less repeated work. The farthest edge shows up a little later
steinlens.directRender=Direct rendering
steinlens.directRender.hint=Draws straight to the window, without the game's intermediate image: a little lighter. Turns off the spectator and F4 effects
steinlens.graphicsApi=API
steinlens.graphicsApi.hint=How the game talks to the graphics card. Vulkan is the default; OpenGL is for when Vulkan does not run. A change counts the next time the game opens
steinlens.graphicsApi.unavailable=Vulkan did not start on this computer (%s), so the game is using OpenGL
steinlens.graphicsApi.reason.no_driver=no Vulkan driver
steinlens.graphicsApi.reason.no_window=the window system refused Vulkan
steinlens.graphicsApi.reason.no_device=no graphics card with Vulkan 1.2
steinlens.graphicsApi.reason.old_driver=graphics driver too old for Vulkan
steinlens.graphicsApi.crashed=The last time the game opened with Vulkan it closed before showing up, so it went back to OpenGL. You can pick Vulkan again here or in the Stein Client
steinlens.graphics=Graphics
steinlens.graphics.fast=Fast
steinlens.graphics.fancy=Fancy

# Video settings topics
steinlens.topic.general=General
steinlens.topic.camera=Camera and players
steinlens.topic.world=World
steinlens.topic.light=Light and shadows
steinlens.topic.sky=Sky and weather
steinlens.topic.textures=Textures
steinlens.topic.players=Players and items
steinlens.topic.performance=Performance
steinlens.rain=Rain
steinlens.rain.hint=Off, rain and snow disappear for you only (no drops and no sound). The weather stays the same on the server
steinlens.chunkFade=Chunk fade-in
steinlens.chunkFade.hint=Chunks that load come out of the fog little by little. Off, they appear at once
steinlens.graphics.hint=The game's modes. Fast makes everything lighter: turns off clouds, rain, smooth lighting and shadows, reduces particles, turns on direct drawing and caps the distance at 8 chunks. Fancy is the game as it ships
steinlens.topic.animations=1.7 animations
steinlens.oldAnimations=1.7 animations
steinlens.oldAnimations.hint=The 1.7 animations, on your screen only: nothing changes for the server. Each part below turns on and off on its own
steinlens.oldBlockHit=Block hitting
steinlens.oldBlockHit.hint=The swing shows even while blocking, eating or drawing a bow, as in 1.7. Animation only: it does not mine or tell the server
steinlens.oldItems=Held items
steinlens.oldItems.hint=Items in hand in first person in the 1.7 position, a little smaller and lower. Blocks do not change
steinlens.oldSwordBlock=Sword blocking
steinlens.oldSwordBlock.hint=The blocking sword in first person at the 1.7 position
steinlens.oldBow=Bow
steinlens.oldBow.hint=The bow in first person at the 1.7 position, idle and drawn
steinlens.oldRod=Fishing rod
steinlens.oldRod.hint=The fishing rod (and the carrot on a stick) in first person at the 1.7 position
steinlens.oldBlockPose=3rd person blocking
steinlens.oldBlockPose.hint=Players blocking with the 1.7 arm and sword, the sword across the body
steinlens.oldArmorHurt=Armor hurt color
steinlens.oldArmorHurt.hint=Armor turns red together with the body when a player or mob takes damage, like in 1.7
steinbridge.bench.title=Stein benchmark: %s (%d of %d). Keyboard and mouse are off; close the window to stop it
steinbridge.bench.preparing=Stein benchmark: preparing the world. Keyboard and mouse are off; close the window to stop it
steinbridge.bench.done=Stein benchmark finished. The report is at %s
steinbridge.bench.failed=Stein benchmark: the report could not be written (%s)
steinbridge.bench.invalid=Some parts ran with the window out of focus, minimized or resized: they are marked in the report
steinlens.hurtShake=Damage shake
steinlens.hurtShake.hint=How much the camera tilts when you take damage, from off to the game's (Default). Only the picture changes: aim and the server do not
steinlens.graphicsApi.restart=Changed: the game opens with %s from the next time. Close and open the game again to use it
steinlens.graphicsApi.forced=Fixed for this session by the start option -Dsteinbridge.gfx.api
steinlens.bloom=Bloom
steinlens.bloom.low=Low
steinlens.bloom.high=High
steinlens.bloom.hint=A soft glow around the brightest parts of the world (sky near the sun, torches, lava). The HUD and menus don't change
steinlens.smoothEdges=Smooth edges
steinlens.smoothEdges.hint=Smooths the jagged outline of blocks, players and items. Textures stay sharp
steinlens.hdr=HDR
steinlens.hdr.hint=On an HDR screen, the lights (sun, torches, lava) shine brighter than the menus' white. Needs Vulkan and HDR turned on in Windows
steinlens.hdrWhite=HDR brightness
steinlens.hdrWhite.hint=How bright the menus' white and the world by day are. Keep it near Windows' "SDR content brightness"
steinlens.hdrPeak=Screen peak
steinlens.hdrPeak.hint=Your screen's highest brightness (in its specs: HDR400, HDR600, HDR1000...). Lights approach it without turning flat white
steinlens.nits=%s nits
steinlens.topic.display=Display and HDR
steinlens.topic.image=Image
steinlens.hdrBlack=HDR shadows
steinlens.hdrBlack.hint=Lightens or deepens the darkest parts. Raise it if dark places turn into a black blot
steinlens.anisotropy=Anisotropy
steinlens.anisotropy.hint=Keeps floors and walls sharp from afar and at an angle. Higher is sharper and heavier. Needs mipmaps (Textures tab)
steinlens.supersample=Shimmer-free pixels
steinlens.supersample.hint=Textures stop flickering from afar and at an angle, and stay sharp up close. Needs mipmaps (Textures tab)
steinlens.sharpen=Sharpness
steinlens.sharpen.hint=Brings out the textures' detail without a bright outline at the edges. Applied on release
steinlens.sharpen.1=Low
steinlens.sharpen.2=Medium
steinlens.sharpen.3=High
steinlens.hdrLook=HDR style
steinlens.hdrLook.stein=Stein
steinlens.hdrLook.natural=Natural
steinlens.hdrLook.hint=Stein: soft colours, a little more vivid, without harsh contrast. Natural: the picture as the game draws it
steinlens.hdrQuality=HDR quality
steinlens.hdrQuality.quick=Quick
steinlens.hdrQuality.max=Maximum
steinlens.hdrQuality.hint=Quick: the same picture at a much lower cost (only the lights use the extra precision). Maximum: the whole picture with extra precision
steinlens.smoothEdges.scaled=With HDR on, it stays off while the render resolution is not Automatic
steinlens.renderScale=Resolution
steinlens.renderScale.auto=Automatic
steinlens.renderScale.hint=Below 100% is lighter; above, sharper and much heavier. The HUD and the menus do not change. Applied on release
steinlens.hdr.unavailable=Unavailable: needs Vulkan and a screen with HDR turned on in Windows' display settings
steinlens.customSky=Custom sky
steinlens.customSky.hint=The sky of resource packs that bring one (the MCPatcher and OptiFine format), over the game's. Layers in the current pack: %s
steinlens.game.renderDistance.hint=How many chunks around you the world is drawn. Farther costs more on the processor and the graphics card. On a server, the limit is what it sends
steinlens.game.framerate.hint=The most frames per second. Unlimited, the graphics card draws as many as it can; with a limit, it runs cooler and uses less power
steinlens.game.vsync.hint=Follows the monitor's refresh: no tearing, but the frame rate stays at the monitor's rate
steinlens.game.fullscreen.hint=The game fills the whole screen, without the window. The same as F11
steinlens.game.guiScale.hint=The size of the HUD, the menus and the text. Auto picks the largest that fits the window
steinlens.game.gamma.hint=Lightens dark places, like caves and the night. It does not change the game's light, only how the picture looks
steinlens.game.smoothLighting.hint=Soft shadows in corners and under blocks. Off is a little lighter
steinlens.game.entityShadows.hint=The round shadow on the ground under players, mobs and items
steinlens.game.clouds.hint=The clouds in the sky: fancy (with volume), fast (flat) or off
steinlens.game.particles.hint=How many particles appear: smoke, hits, potions, breaking blocks. Fewer helps in crowded fights
steinlens.game.mipmap.hint=Smaller versions of the textures for what is far away: removes noise and flicker. Applied on release, since it reloads the textures (takes a few seconds)
steinlens.game.blockAlternatives.hint=Random variations of some blocks' textures (grass, stone...), so the ground does not look repeated
steinlens.game.fov.hint=How much you see to the sides. Wider shows more, with things looking farther away
steinlens.game.viewBobbing.hint=The camera sways as you walk
steinlens.game.vbo.hint=Keeps the terrain in the graphics card's memory. On is faster on almost every computer
steinlens.renderScale.now=Now: %s, %s%% of the window (%s)
steinlens.renderScale.nowAuto=Now: automatic, %s (the window's size)
steinlens.renderScale.autoShort=Auto
